config REMOTEID_BLE_TX_INTERVAL_MS
    int "BLE advertisement rotation interval (ms)"
    default 250
    range 100 260
    depends on REMOTEID_TRANSPORT_BLE || REMOTEID_TRANSPORT_BLE5_LONG_RANGE
    help
        Interval between BLE advertisement payload updates. BLE 5 Long Range
        sends the whole Message Pack (every message) once per interval. For
        BLE 4 legacy advertising, one message per interval: the schedule has
        9 slots (Location and System in every third slot) plus up to four
        100 ms authentication slots between them. At the 260 ms maximum
        Location and System are still sent at least once per second
        (3 x 260 + 200 = 980 ms) and every other message at least every 3 s
        (9 x 260 + 400 = 2740 ms); larger values would break those rates.

config REMOTEID_INDICATOR_RGB_ENABLE
    bool "Enable onboard RGB status indicator"
    default n
    help
        Drive a board-mounted addressable RGB LED, typically WS2812/SK6812, as
        a local firmware status indicator. Before Remote ID is operational it
        shows status/error indications. After transports have started and valid
        identity is present, it switches to the configured operational flash
        pattern. This is separate from the TX status LED pulse output.

if REMOTEID_INDICATOR_RGB_ENABLE

